  "_doc": "How the ground is painted (js/client/render/ground.js is the one reader; tools/bake-ground.mjs bakes `layers` into img/ground/*.webp). `layers`: the painted surfaces in order (the first eight are the splat channels, the ninth is rock, laid on by slope in the shader); `metres` = how many metres one repeat covers; `tone` × `bright` multiply the picture (warm it, lift it); `low` = the 1-texel stand-in drawn until the pictures load. `biomes`: which layer each terrain biome paints. `towns`: paving per town (squares, streets = the roads inside the town, yards round buildings and listed props). `fields`: the crops planted in map.json's fields (a field is cut into strips across its long side, one crop per strip) and their fence. `grass`: the tufts that grow round the camera per quality setting.",
